    "summary": "In-sample 2025 excess is a broad, shallow, mostly-POSITIVE plateau (avg +0.58%, peak +1.15% near T-20..T-30 -> T-7) but NO cell reaches t>1.96 (max t=1.89) and only 1/92 clears the one-sided p<0.05 bar (t>1.645) -- FEWER than the ~4.6 false positives expected by chance. The lone 3-cell \"stable region\" is contiguous only because overlapping windows force smoothness. It FLIPS to -0.48% (t=-0.65, 0/3 cells positive) on the 2026 hold-out; the 2025 and 2026 surfaces are uncorrelated (r=0.045); 2026 has 0/92 cells at t>1.5. Conclusion: no exploitable timing edge -- the surface is noise around a small, 2025-specific, non-recurring drift."
  }
